        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Cohomology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COHOMOLOGY GROUP: Hⁿ(X; R) = Zⁿ/Bⁿ"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COHOMOLOGY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "08-COHOMOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:topology:08-cohomology, git-history:topology:08-cohomology]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "current_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:cohomology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Cohomology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "UNIVERSAL COEFFICIENT THEOREM:\n  0 → Ext¹(Hₙ₋₁(X;Z), Z) → Hⁿ(X;Z) → Hom(Hₙ(X;Z), Z) → 0.\n  This sequence splits (non-naturally)."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COHOMOLOGY.md#013",
      "path": [
        "08-COHOMOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:topology:08-cohomology, git-history:topology:08-cohomology]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "current_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:cohomology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Cohomology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Ext¹(Z, Z) = 0, Ext¹(Z/n, Z) = Z/n, Ext¹(free, Z) = 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COHOMOLOGY.md#014",
      "path": [
        "08-COHOMOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:topology:08-cohomology, git-history:topology:08-cohomology]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "current_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:cohomology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Cohomology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY CONSEQUENCE: If all homology groups are torsion-free (free abelian),\n  then Hⁿ(X;Z) ≅ Hₙ(X;Z). (Homology and cohomology groups agree when free.)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-COHOMOLOGY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "08-COHOMOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:topology:08-cohomology, git-history:topology:08-cohomology]",
        "canonical_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "current_path": "topology/08-COHOMOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:topology:cohomology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "topology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[cohomology]",
        "section": "topology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Cohomology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "When there's torsion: cohomology can have torsion one degree higher.\n  Example: RP²:\n    H₁(RP²;Z) = Z/2 → Ext¹(Z/2, Z) = Z/2 appears in H²(RP²;Z).\n    So H²(RP²;Z) = Z/2, even though H₂(RP²;Z) = 0.\n```"
    },
